  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-17T10:48:55.066Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With the discussion of effectiveness of crunch compression, and android build size I think it's necessary to show the size of the last build.\n\nParticularly I want to see build size for android. Right now if I want to see how large my build is for android I have to select build and publish, but if I'm just comparing compression options I don't want to actually try and upload to VRChat. I get that \"build and test\" is not possible for Quest, but one thing I can do on PC is I know where VRChat stores the build and test output for the client to pick up, so I can easily peek at asset bundle size without spamming VRChat.\n\nOn a PC the only way to get a quest size right now is to either exceed 10MB or upload to VRChat, and pester a quest user to say the number\n\nAlso for the editor.log file it keeps track of a percentage of the asset bundle, I'd like to know how small the file is in the bundle in bytes, not percentage.",
